# Implement the Full Syslog-NG Logging and Monitoring Topology

## Objective

This guide changes the current environment so that logs are:

1. Received by **Syslog-NG** on `192.168.1.176`.
2. Stored on local disk by port, source IP, and date.
3. Forwarded to **Grafana Alloy**.
4. Stored in **Loki**.
5. Viewed in **Grafana**.
6. Compressed and deleted according to retention.

```text
VM2 rsyslog
   │ TCP 1514
   ▼
Syslog-NG on 192.168.1.176
   ├──► /var/log/remote/port-1514/<source-IP>/<year>/<month>/<day>/messages.log
   └──► Alloy on 127.0.0.1:2514
            ▼
           Loki
            ▼
          Grafana
```

VM2 continues sending to:

```text
192.168.1.176:1514
```

All remaining changes are made on the monitoring server unless stated otherwise.

